{
  "sn46.54:0.1": "Linked Discourses 46.54 ",
  "sn46.54:0.2": "6. Discussion ",
  "sn46.54:0.3": "Full of Love ",
  "sn46.54:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying in the land of the Koliyans, where they have a town named Haliddavasana. ",
  "sn46.54:1.2": "Then several mendicants robed up in the morning and, taking their bowls and robes, entered Haliddavasana for alms. ",
  "sn46.54:1.3": "Then it occurred to them, ",
  "sn46.54:1.4": "“It’s too early to wander for alms in Haliddavasana. ",
  "sn46.54:1.5": "Why don’t we visit the monastery for the wanderers of other religions?” ",
  "sn46.54:2.1": "Then they went to the monastery for the wanderers of other religions and exchanged greetings with the wanderers there. ",
  "sn46.54:2.2": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, they sat down to one side. The wanderers said to them: ",
  "sn46.54:3.1": "“Reverends, the ascetic Gotama teaches his disciples like this: ",
  "sn46.54:3.2": "‘Come, mendicants, give up these five hindrances, corruptions of the heart that weaken wisdom, and meditate spreading a heart full of love to one direction, and to the second, and to the third, and to the fourth. In the same way above, below, across, everywhere, all around, spread a heart full of love to the whole world—abundant, expansive, limitless, free of enmity and ill will. ",
  "sn46.54:3.3": "Meditate spreading a heart full of compassion to one direction, and to the second, and to the third, and to the fourth. In the same way above, below, 